## Context

Filed from ticket 0183 (the read-and-judge test-audit-llm skill). Ticket 0226
deferred a "pass-shape dedup (runPass/expandRules extraction)" to 0183, on the
theory that the next test-quality lens would pay for a shared abstraction.

While building 0183, that cross-skill extraction was determined **mechanically
impossible**:
- Workflow scripts run in a sandbox with **no module imports** (no `require`, no
  `import`, no `process`); a `skills/_shared` does not and cannot exist.
- maw-audit's `expandRules`-style token substitution (`<RUN_TEST>`,
  `<MUTATION_HEURISTICS>`, `<TAGS>`, `<SRC_DIR>`) is **mutation-specific** —
  test-audit-llm executes nothing, so it has no test command, no pairing table,
  no mutation/handcuff heuristics to template, and a single fan-out (no
  multi-pass `runPass` shape to share).

So the cross-skill abstraction 0226 imagined has no surface. The **legitimate
residue** is purely maw-audit-INTERNAL: three near-identical rule templaters —
`applyRules` (fang), `handcuffRules`, `scopeRules` in
`skills/maw-audit/maw-audit.js` — each doing the same `<TOKEN>`-replacement over
a different RULES string. They can collapse into one `expandRules(rulesText,
tags)` helper that substitutes the common tokens, with each pass passing its own
RULES body + any pass-specific token.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `applyRules` / `handcuffRules` / `scopeRules` collapsed into one
      `expandRules(rulesText, tags)` in `skills/maw-audit/maw-audit.js`.
- [ ] Behavior-preserving: the generated prompts are byte-identical to before
      (the substitution set per pass is unchanged).
- [ ] `tests/test_maw_audit_skill.py` still passes (the structural assertions on
      each pass's prompt content are unaffected); fixtures still pass.
- [ ] `make check` and `make check-fast` pass.

## Notes
This is a pure internal refactor of ONE skill — NOT the cross-skill extraction
0226 hypothesised (that is impossible; see Context). Gated on the maw-audit
fixtures and structural tests still passing.
